  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Hindustan Unilever Limited vs The State Of Bihar on 2 February, 2017 Author: Vinod Kumar Sinha",
    "facts": "The persecution story in short is that the Food Inspector Mr. Keshari Mohan Jha visited M/S Keshri Bhandar, a shop of Pithiya Gachhi in the district of Samastipur on 16.5.2006 and took sample of Annapurna Iodized Salt and sent it to Public Analyst, Bihar, Patna on 17.6.2006 and received Report No.2178/PFA/2006 dated 8th July, 2006 that \"Logo for veg. is not fixed on proper site of the label\" hence, \"the sample of Annapurana Iodized Salt violates the labeling provisions of PF Rules, 1955 regarding Logo so it is misbranded\", on the basis of the aforesaid report, G.O. Case No.06 of 2006 Trial No.2214 of 2013 was instituted",
    "arguments": "It is submitted on behalf of the petitioner that except the allegation that \"logo for veg. is not fixed on proper site of the label\" and \"the sample of Annapurana Iodized Salt violates the labeling provisions of P.F.A. Rules, 1955 regarding logo so it is misbranded\", there is no other allegation against him-company, as appears from Annexure-1& 2 of the application, however, this Hon'ble Court vide judgment in the case of Vinita Bali - Vrs.- The State of Bihar reported in (2008) (4) PLJR 135 has already [LEAKAGE_MASK] the order on the basis of such type of allegation and thereafter in several cases, this Hon'ble Court has held that in absence of any statement as to where such Logo has to be affixed, the petitioner can not be prosecuted for want of such requirement of the Rule under the P.F.A. Act. As such the order taking cognizance by the Sub- divisional Judicial Magistrate, Samastipur is bad in law and fit to be [LEAKAGE_MASK]. Heard learned A.P.P. also, who could not controvert the aforesaid fact that in a similar circumstances a large number of cases order taking cognizance has been [LEAKAGE_MASK] for prosecution for not placing the logo on the proper place.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "It is submitted on behalf of the petitioner that except the allegation that \"logo for veg. is not fixed on proper site of the label\" and \"the sample of Annapurana Iodized Salt violates the labeling provisions of P.F.A. Rules, 1955 regarding logo so it is misbranded\", there is no other allegation against him-company, as appears from Annexure-1& 2 of the application, however, this Hon'ble Court vide judgment in the case of Vinita Bali - Vrs.- The State of Bihar reported in (2008) (4) PLJR 135 has already [LEAKAGE_MASK] the order on the basis of such type of allegation and thereafter in several cases, this Hon'ble Court has held that in absence of any statement as to where such Logo has to be affixed, the petitioner can not be prosecuted for want of such requirement of the Rule under the P.F.A. Act. As such the order taking cognizance by the Sub- divisional Judicial Magistrate, Samastipur is bad in law and fit to be [LEAKAGE_MASK]. Heard learned A.P.P. also, who could not controvert the aforesaid fact that in a similar circumstances a large number of cases order taking cognizance has been [LEAKAGE_MASK] for prosecution for not placing the logo on the proper place.",
